A||||3||XDrewX||Power window / lock / mirror conversion||||5||
Z||000000||XDrewX||11-05-2001||11:07 PM||||Are all cars pre wired for these.<P>This is my plan.<P>I would like to remove the entire door from the car that has standard windows/locks/mirrors and replace it with an entire door which does have power windows/locks/mirrors.<P><BR>Now my question, after doing this door switch, can I just " PLUG IN " the power window/door/mirrors.<P>I know I would have to also remove the window/mirror switch plate.  Would this be plug and play also.<P><BR>Thanks<P>Andrew<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||11-05-2001||11:15 PM||||The wiring is not included in non-power cars. The harnesses are seperate and can be removed from the donor car and put in yours without any cutting/splicing. Don't forget the circuit breaker in the fuse box.<P>"Some disassembly required". You will need to remove the dash and a lot of the center console to route the wires. It helps if you take the wiring out of the donor car yourself so you know how it goes. The console switches are plug and play once you get the harness in.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-06-2001||05:08 AM||||And since you're going to have a door panel with that manual mirror joystick cutout on the top, why not try my alternate mirror switch mod.  One less wiring harness to run, too.  See the article in Ogres cave under "Make Me".||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||11-06-2001||06:24 AM||||I'm doing the same thing, what everybody else says is what I've found so far...<BR>I'm doing what Ogre suggested with the power mirror thing. I found a cool switch from a Merkur at the boneyard, it fits perfectly in the original driver's door location (maybe it's the same switch!)<BR>Good luck and keep posting your progress...<P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||1
